-- ============================================================
-- XI. DESERT CROWN RELIQUARY (沙王陵)
-- ============================================================

update wf_user.my_frames
set
    cultivation_color    = '#D4A017',
    cultivation_school   = 'Desert Crown Reliquary',
    cultivation_identity = 'Malik',
    cultivation_art      = 'Pharaoh Sand Dao of the Deshret Crown',
    cultivation_doctrine = $doc$Inaros Prime's name is shared by two historical pharaohs of the 26th and 27th Dynasties -- rulers whose reign defined the late period of Egyptian royal authority, the kings who held the Deshret Crown when the old world was ending and kept it held. The Desert Crown Reliquary is built entirely around this lineage: the cultivation practice of the god-king, the pharaoh whose authority is not granted by armies but by the desert itself. Desiccation does not blind. It commands the sand -- the Deshret Crown's first assertion of territorial authority, the desert answering its king. Devour does not incapacitate. It entombs -- the sarcophagus function that Egyptian royal theology treated as transformation rather than death, the cultivator demonstrating that Inaros Prime's domain includes the boundary between living and preserved. Sandstorm does not deal damage. It expresses sovereignty -- the pharaoh making the claim that this airspace is the desert's airspace, and the desert belongs to Inaros Prime. Scarab Swarm does not apply a debuff. It consecrates -- the sacred scarab of Egyptian tradition employed as both biological weapon and cultural statement, the god-king whose cultivation is inseparable from his theology. With 2,415 base health and no shields, Inaros Prime does not survive because he is defended. He survives because the desert does not kill its pharaoh.$doc$
where build_title = 'Malik';


-- ============================================================
-- XII. IRONCLAD MOUNTAIN HALL (玄铁山殿)
-- ============================================================

update wf_user.my_frames
set
    cultivation_color    = '#B89F50',
    cultivation_school   = 'Ironclad Mountain Hall',
    cultivation_identity = 'Krono Titan',
    cultivation_art      = 'Iron Hide Dao of the Charging Titan',
    cultivation_doctrine = $doc$Rhino Prime is the Ironclad Mountain Hall's founding argument: that the simplest cultivation doctrine, executed without compromise, produces power that more sophisticated practitioners spend their entire careers trying to surpass. He does not have a complex lore lineage. He has Iron Skin -- the Overguard of a cultivator who decided that the most efficient defensive technology is not adaptability or avoidance but the willingness to simply absorb more than the enemy can produce. Rhino Charge does not provide mobility. It is a weapon with a movement mechanic attached: the Charging Titan's fundamental combat statement, that a 200-kilogram mass moving at speed is a force multiplier that no ability description fully captures. Roar does not buff damage. It broadcasts -- the sound of the Ironclad Mountain Hall's founding principle, a noise that functions as a tactical asset because everything in range that hears it recalibrates its threat assessment. Rhino Stomp does not apply a time slow. It concludes the Iron Hide Dao's argument: the Charging Titan arriving at his destination, the ground registering that something has landed, time having opinions about the force involved. The Ironclad Mountain Hall was built for Rhino Prime, and Rhino Prime was built for the Mountain Hall, and neither of them is apologizing for it.$doc$
where build_title = 'Krono Titan';

update wf_user.my_frames
set
    cultivation_color    = '#6B4423',
    cultivation_school   = 'Ironclad Mountain Hall',
    cultivation_identity = 'Mountain King',
    cultivation_art      = 'Earthbound Titan Dao of the Petrified Gaze',
    cultivation_doctrine = $doc$Atlas Prime's cultivation lineage runs through two mythological traditions simultaneously: the Greek Titan Atlas who holds the world on his shoulders, and the Medusa-adjacent Petrified Gaze that transforms contact into stone. The Earthbound Titan Dao treats both as expressions of the same principle -- that the cultivator who is most completely connected to the earth beneath them has access to a form of power that the sky-bound and water-bound and fire-bound traditions cannot reach, because the earth does not move and the cultivator who IS the earth shares that permanence. Landslide does not charge. It conducts geological time at combat speed -- the mountain expressing its mass as a fist, the Earthbound Titan demonstrating that stone does not need momentum because it has weight. Tectonics does not summon a boulder. It remembers -- Atlas Prime's Greek lineage reasserting that walls of stone are the original defensive architecture. Petrify does not crowd control. It extends the Gaze -- the Mountain King looking at something and finding that the earth agrees it should stop. Rumblers does not summon golems. It delegates -- the Earthbound Titan calling the stone itself to serve, the mountain sending pieces of itself because the king does not walk everywhere himself.$doc$
where build_title = 'Mountain King';

update wf_user.my_frames
set
    cultivation_color    = '#5A3A1B',
    cultivation_school   = 'Ironclad Mountain Hall',
    cultivation_identity = 'Gourmand Titan',
    cultivation_art      = 'Devouring Oni Dao of the Insatiable Belly',
    cultivation_doctrine = $doc$Grendel Prime's cultivation lineage is the Beowulf poem's cannibal giant filtered through the Japanese Oni -- the mountain demon who feasts because feasting is the Ironclad Mountain Hall's most direct form of cultivation. His codename is Oni, and the Devouring Oni Dao makes no attempt to refine this into something more palatable: Grendel Prime eats enemies, and eating enemies is his cultivation practice. Feast does not crowd control. It feeds -- Grendel Prime consuming enemies and adding their mass to his own, the +250 armor per devoured enemy in his gut representing the most literal interpretation of the Ironclad Mountain Hall's core principle that the strongest cultivator is the one who has absorbed the most. Nourish does not apply an energy buff. It metabolizes -- the Devouring Oni converting what he has eaten into applicable force, the cultivator as digestive system. Regurgitate does not deal damage. It conducts a culinary critique -- Grendel Prime returning undigested enemies as projectiles, the Insatiable Belly rendering its verdict on what it has consumed. Pulverize does not roll. It feasts in motion -- the Gourmand Titan as a rolling biomass event, collecting and converting at speed, the Oni demon's fundamental truth: that everything Grendel Prime touches is potential food, and potential food is potential strength.$doc$
where build_title = 'Gourmand Titan';

update wf_user.my_frames
set
    cultivation_color    = '#8B0000',
    cultivation_school   = 'Ironclad Mountain Hall',
    cultivation_identity = 'E.N.D',
    cultivation_art      = 'Chromatic Dragon Dao of the Vex Pelt',
    cultivation_doctrine = $doc$Chroma Prime's cultivation lineage is the Dungeons and Dragons Chromatic Dragon -- the apex predator of the Ironclad Mountain Hall, the elemental-master cultivator who has claimed the right to every element simultaneously by mastering each one individually. His spectral energy color determines his element: red for Fire, blue for Cold, yellow for Electricity, white for Toxin. The Chromatic Dragon Dao treats this as the Hall's highest teaching: that the cultivator who can access all four elements without committing to one has achieved a form of tactical flexibility that the mono-element traditions cannot match. Spectral Scream does not deal damage. It breathes -- the dragon's breath weapon, here tuned to whatever element Chroma Prime is currently expressing. Elemental Ward does not buff the squad. It radiates -- the Dragon Pelt expressing its element outward, the Chromatic Dragon making its nature into an environmental condition. Vex Armor does not grant stacking damage and armor bonuses. It stacks fury -- the moment when Chroma Prime takes damage, the Dragon responds by becoming angrier and harder, the Vex Pelt's fundamental property being that it improves under assault. Effigy does not summon a decoy. It sheds the Dragon Pelt entirely -- leaving it to fight independently while Chroma Prime operates in his debuffed but liberated state, the E.N.D demonstrating that even without his pelt, the Chromatic Dragon is not finished.$doc$
where build_title = 'E.N.D';


-- ============================================================
-- XIII. PHANTOM THEATER CONSERVATORY
-- ============================================================

update wf_user.my_frames
set
    cultivation_color    = '#E5B8E5',
    cultivation_school   = 'Phantom Theater Conservatory',
    cultivation_identity = 'Sound Sovereign',
    cultivation_art      = 'Mandachord Resonance Dao of the Pentatonic Bard',
    cultivation_doctrine = $doc$Octavia Prime is the Phantom Theater Conservatory's empress -- the cultivator who established the School's foundational premise that music is not an accompaniment to combat but its own form of force, and that the practitioner who has mastered the Mandachord has access to a form of battlefield control that weapon-users cannot conceptualize because it operates at the frequency level rather than the kinetic level. The Mandachord is a step-sequencer tuned to the Pentatonic-D-minor scale, and Octavia Prime's four abilities are instruments: Mallet is the percussion section, a damage-dealing resonator that grows stronger the more the enemy attacks it, converting hostility into amplitude. Resonator is the bass line, a rolling sphere that attracts enemies with its frequency before Mallet concludes the arrangement. Metronome is the tempo track, rewarding allies who move in rhythm with the Mandachord's beat with buffs that the Pentatonic Bard Dao describes as the natural result of existing in correct relationship with the music. Amp is the master volume, and when Octavia Prime turns it up, the Resonance Dao's central teaching becomes environmental law: in the Sound Sovereign's concert hall, the music is not background. The music IS the outcome.$doc$
where build_title = 'Sound Sovereign';

update wf_user.my_frames
set
    cultivation_color    = '#003366',
    cultivation_school   = 'Phantom Theater Conservatory',
    cultivation_identity = 'Ethereal Sage',
    cultivation_art      = 'Tomeweaver Dao of the Inferno-Paradiso Verses',
    cultivation_doctrine = $doc$Dante is named after Dante Alighieri, the author of the Divine Comedy -- the Inferno, Purgatorio, and Paradiso -- and his cultivation practice is a direct translation of the poem's structure into Warframe mechanics. His abilities alternate between Light Verse and Dark Verse, Heaven and Hell, the Tomeweaver cycling through the Divine Comedy's three canticles as combat resources. Noctua does not deal damage. It writes -- the poet's pen, the Tomeweaver recording the battlefield's state before the verses begin. Pageflight does not provide utility. It conducts the Inferno's opening movement: the descent into the selva oscura, the dark wood, where Dante lost his way and found his guide. Tragedy does not apply a debuff. It concludes the Dark Verse -- the Inferno canticle completing, the weight of every accumulated dark effect converted into a single devastating reckoning. Triumph does not heal or generate Overguard. It concludes the Light Verse -- the Paradiso canticle completing, the Divine Comedy's promise that suffering has a terminal point and that point is transcendence. The Tomeweaver Dao teaches that the scribe-mage does not fight with spells. He fights with narrative -- and the cultivator who controls the story controls how it ends.$doc$
where build_title = 'Ethereal Sage';


-- ============================================================
-- XIV. CHRONOS ENGINEERING BUREAU (时械殿)
-- ============================================================

update wf_user.my_frames
set
    cultivation_color    = '#2EBFA5',
    cultivation_school   = 'Chronos Engineering Bureau',
    cultivation_identity = 'Time Divine',
    cultivation_art      = 'Protean Chrono Dao of the Anchored Rewind',
    cultivation_doctrine = $doc$Protea Prime's Greek lineage is Proteus -- the shapeshifter, the old man of the sea who changes form continuously to avoid being held to a single answer. The Chronos Engineering Bureau takes this shapeshifting and applies it to the dimension of time rather than form, producing the Protean Chrono Dao: the cultivation practice of a cultivator who has learned that the most powerful engineering is not building forward but anchoring backward. Grenade Fan does not throw grenades. It deploys gadgets -- Protea Prime's shapeshifting expressed as tactical versatility, the Protean principle that the cultivator who can produce multiple tool types simultaneously is not committing to a single solution. Blaze Artillery does not deal sustained damage. It engineers a turret -- the Chronos Bureau's fixed-point combat doctrine, power that does not require the cultivator's continuous attention because it has been correctly built. Dispensary does not generate resources. It manufactures -- the Protean Chrono Dao's fundamental technique, producing what the squad needs rather than finding it. Temporal Anchor is not an ultimate ability. It is a temporal engineering operation: Protea Prime placing a save-point in time, fighting forward for fifteen seconds, and then rewinding to the anchor while retaining all the energy she generated in the interval. The Protean Chrono Dao teaches that the engineer's advantage over the warrior is that the engineer can undo mistakes. Protea Prime has made this into a combat art.$doc$
where build_title = 'Time Divine';

update wf_user.my_frames
set
    cultivation_color    = '#1F3A93',
    cultivation_school   = 'Chronos Engineering Bureau',
    cultivation_identity = 'AOE Engineer',
    cultivation_art      = 'Bastille Siegecraft Dao of the Star-Fort Marshal',
    cultivation_doctrine = $doc$Vauban Prime is named after Sebastien Le Prestre de Vauban, the 17th-century Marshal of France who revolutionized military fortification and invented the star-fort design -- the geometric defensive architecture that dominated European warfare for two centuries. The Bastille Siegecraft Dao takes Vauban's engineering genius and applies it to mobile combat, producing the Chronos Engineering Bureau's most militarily precise practitioner: the cultivator who does not fight the enemy so much as he engineers the conditions under which the enemy cannot effectively fight back. Tesla Nervos does not deal damage. It engineers a persistent area-denial system -- the star-fort's outer perimeter, mines that follow and stun. Minelayer does not provide utility. It deploys the Bureau's tactical architecture: Nail Grenades for armor strip, Bouncing Bastille for crowd control deployment, Overdriver for ally enhancement, Flechette Orb for sustained area denial. Bastille does not suspend enemies. It constructs -- the star-fort made real, the Vauban design's fundamental promise that the enclosed space belongs to the engineer and not the army outside it. Photon Strike does not deal orbital damage. It calls the Marshal's reserve -- the equivalent of Vauban's artillery support, the Bureau's answer to the question of what happens when the star-fort's walls are insufficient: you call the orbital cannon.$doc$
where build_title = 'AOE Engineer';

update wf_user.my_frames
set
    cultivation_color    = '#FFC107',
    cultivation_school   = 'Chronos Engineering Bureau',
    cultivation_identity = 'Lone Star',
    cultivation_art      = 'Peacemaker Gunslinger Dao of the High Noon Topaz',
    cultivation_doctrine = $doc$Mesa Prime's cultivation lineage runs through the Colt Peacemaker, the Old West gunslinger tradition, and the specific mythological figure of the lawman who stands in the street at high noon and does not draw first but draws fastest. The Peacemaker Gunslinger Dao treats this as a complete cultivation philosophy: the gunfighter's art is not aggression but precision, not speed but the specific speed that matters -- the moment between the enemy's intention and Mesas's response. Ballistic Battery does not charge damage. It loads -- the gunslinger ensuring that when the draw comes, the first shot carries the full weight of what came before it. Shooting Gallery does not buff allies and confuse enemies. It manages the saloon -- the Lone Star maintaining situational control of everyone in range, ensuring that the Chronos Engineering Bureau's most offensive practitioner is never fighting a fair fight because fair fights are for people who cannot engineer their circumstances. Shatter Shield does not provide damage reduction. It prepares the draw -- the gunslinger putting on the vest, the Lone Star ensuring she will still be standing when Peacemaker completes. Peacemaker does not channel. It draws -- the Colt Peacemaker brought to bear at High Noon speed, the Regulators spinning into existence as the extensions of a combat doctrine so complete that Mesa Prime's hands are no longer the limiting factor. Only her aim is.$doc$
where build_title = 'Lone Star';

update wf_user.my_frames
set
    cultivation_color    = '#4A6FA5',
    cultivation_school   = 'Chronos Engineering Bureau',
    cultivation_identity = 'Best Unseen Shooter',
    cultivation_art      = 'Frumentarius Sniper Dao of the Practiced Eye',
    cultivation_doctrine = $doc$Cyte-09's cultivation lineage is the Roman frumentarii -- the imperial intelligence service, the spy-soldiers who operated behind enemy lines collecting grain (frumentum) as cover while conducting espionage and assassination. The Frumentarius Sniper Dao takes this lineage and refines it through the Chronos Engineering Bureau's precision ethos: the cultivator who has decided that every engagement should be resolved from a position of complete informational superiority before the enemy knows the engagement has begun. Neutralizer is not a sniper's exalted weapon. It is the frumentarius's terminal instrument -- the shot that ends the intelligence operation, delivered from the position that perfect reconnaissance has identified as optimal. Evade does not grant invisibility. It grants invisibility on weak-point kills specifically -- the Practiced Eye rewarding precision with the ability to vanish, the spy-assassin completing an operation and stepping back into the information layer. The Frumentarius Sniper Dao's relationship to Mesa Prime's Peacemaker Dao is precisely the relationship of the sniper to the gunfighter: same tradition of marksman cultivation, different ranges, different operational philosophies. Mesa Prime fights at High Noon. Cyte-09 was never in the street.$doc$
where build_title = 'Best Unseen Shooter';

update wf_user.my_frames
set
    cultivation_color    = '#D62828',
    cultivation_school   = 'Chronos Engineering Bureau',
    cultivation_identity = 'Endurant Saintess',
    cultivation_art      = 'Five-Fates Dice Dao of the Plum-Blossom Oracle',
    cultivation_doctrine = $doc$Koumei's cultivation lineage is the Shinto miko -- the shrine maiden who interprets omens, conducts ritual, and serves as the intermediary between the mortal world and the divine one. But Koumei's miko practice is conducted through dice, and her dice produce Omikuji -- the paper fortune strips drawn at Japanese shrines that assign each supplicant a fate category from Great Blessing to Great Curse. The Five-Fates Dice Dao treats this as the Chronos Engineering Bureau's most unconventional but most complete engineering practice: the cultivator who has learned to engineer probability rather than outcomes. Seijundo does not apply effects. It reads the Omikuji -- the dice falling, the fate strips unfurling, the Plum-Blossom Oracle determining what this moment's probability field looks like. Kazegiri does not deal damage. It conducts a Bunraku performance -- the traditional Japanese puppet theater in which the puppeteers are visible but the audience agrees to see the puppet as real, here inverted: the enemy is real but Koumei makes them see something else. Shadow's Trinity is the jackpot state -- triple six on the dice, the Great Blessing fate strip, the moment when the Endurant Saintess's probability engineering completes and the field collapses into the outcome she has been cultivating across the entire encounter.$doc$
where build_title = 'Endurant Saintess';

update wf_user.my_frames
set
    cultivation_color    = '#DC143C',
    cultivation_school   = 'Chronos Engineering Bureau',
    cultivation_identity = 'Devil',
    cultivation_art      = 'Brimstone Lucifer Dao of the Triadic Legion',
    cultivation_doctrine = $doc$Uriel is the Chronos Engineering Bureau's moral inversion -- the devil in the engineering school, the infernal summoner whose cultivation practice is the structural inverse of the Hallowed Path of Heaven's Light. Where Harrow Prime bleeds for devotion and Baruuk Prime restrains for discipline, Uriel burns for dominion. His name is the Vice Regent Roathe's designation, and his demonic legion -- Catenach, Gulphagor, Vythelas -- are not summoned allies but drafted lieutenants, the Triadic Legion that the Brimstone Lucifer Dao calls the minimum viable infernal hierarchy. The Bureau includes Uriel not despite this inversion but because of it: the Chronos Engineering Bureau has always understood that engineering is morally neutral, that the same organizational genius that builds star-forts can build hellfire rings, that management of a demonic legion requires the same systematic precision as management of a satellite cannon. Uriel does not summon. He administers -- the devil's real power being not the fire but the bureaucracy, the infernal hierarchy that ensures the fire goes exactly where the Triadic Legion's logistics have determined it should go. The Brimstone Lucifer Dao is the Hallowed Path's shadow curriculum, and Uriel is its valedictorian.$doc$
where build_title = 'Devil';
